          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gc8a412ce97f0a7b02299c860d78d46ff" title="Question 14">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>67506,47044,20865,57883</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the term for using someone else's words without acknowledging the source?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="67506">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Plagiarism</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="47044">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Paraphrasing</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="20865">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Summarizing</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="57883">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Citing</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">67506</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="67506_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">47044</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="47044_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">20865</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="20865_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">57883</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="57883_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">67506</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="67506_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Plagiarism is the practice of using someone else's words without acknowledging the source. Plagiarism is a serious academic integrity violation that can occur with direct quotations, paraphrased material, and summarized ideas if the source is not properly cited.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="47044_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Paraphrasing is restating someone's ideas in your own words, but it still requires a citation. Summarizing condenses as a source to its main ideas, but it also requires a citation. Citing is the act of giving proper credit to a source, which is the exact opposite of plagiarism. All three of these practices, done correctly, help writers avoid plagiarism.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="20865_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Paraphrasing is restating someone's ideas in your own words, but it still requires a citation. Summarizing condenses as a source to its main ideas, but it also requires a citation. Citing is the act of giving proper credit to a source, which is the exact opposite of plagiarism. All three of these practices, done correctly, help writers avoid plagiarism.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="57883_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Paraphrasing is restating someone's ideas in your own words, but it still requires a citation. Summarizing condenses as a source to its main ideas, but it also requires a citation. Citing is the act of giving proper credit to a source, which is the exact opposite of plagiarism. All three of these practices, done correctly, help writers avoid plagiarism.</mattext>
          </material>
