          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">47600</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="47600_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">11807</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="11807_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">91716</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="91716_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">9558</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="9558_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Revising and editing your paper is the last step in the six-step research writing process. During this step, you examine the paper's overall structure, unity, and cohesion, then check for proper spelling, grammar, punctuation, mechanics, and formatting.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="47600_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Drafting your paper is Step 5, not the final step. Organizing research and ideas is Step 4. Conducting research is Step 3. All of these steps occur before revision and editing. A paper is not complete until it has been carefully reviewed and polished.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="11807_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Drafting your paper is Step 5, not the final step. Organizing research and ideas is Step 4. Conducting research is Step 3. All of these steps occur before revision and editing. A paper is not complete until it has been carefully reviewed and polished.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="91716_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Drafting your paper is Step 5, not the final step. Organizing research and ideas is Step 4. Conducting research is Step 3. All of these steps occur before revision and editing. A paper is not complete until it has been carefully reviewed and polished.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g540e5a0cd69c1ed50e8e5850033d3d98" title="Question 17">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>19182,7131,34310,94967</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;Which domain extension often indicates a more reliable website for academic research?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="19182">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">.edu</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="7131">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">.com</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="34310">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">.net</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="94967">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">.biz</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">19182</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="19182_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">7131</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="7131_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">34310</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="34310_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">94967</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="94967_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">19182</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="19182_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The .edu domain extension often indicates a more reliable website for academic research. Educational institutions, governmental agencies (.gov), and established organizations (.org) tend to produce more credible content than commercial websites.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="7131_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The .com, .net, and .biz extensions are commonly used by commercial businesses and individuals. These sites may be well-designed and popular, but popularity does not equal accuracy. Search engine results rank sites by how often they are visited, not by how reliable their information is. Always evaluate each source on its own merits regardless of its domain.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="34310_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The .com, .net, and .biz extensions are commonly used by commercial businesses and individuals. These sites may be well-designed and popular, but popularity does not equal accuracy. Search engine results rank sites by how often they are visited, not by how reliable their information is. Always evaluate each source on its own merits regardless of its domain.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="94967_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The .com, .net, and .biz extensions are commonly used by commercial businesses and individuals. These sites may be well-designed and popular, but popularity does not equal accuracy. Search engine results rank sites by how often they are visited, not by how reliable their information is. Always evaluate each source on its own merits regardless of its domain.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g86bec1428ded3ec24553d44d88a57595" title="Question 18">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>60426,10823,67663,89609</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What does it mean to cite a source?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="60426">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To acknowledge the source of information you used in your work</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="10823">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To copy text directly from a source into your paper</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="67663">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To search for a source using a library database</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="89609">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To summarize the main points of a source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">60426</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="60426_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">10823</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="10823_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">67663</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="67663_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">89609</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="89609_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">60426</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="60426_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">To cite a source means to acknowledge the source of information you used in your work. Proper citation gives credit to the original author and allows readers to locate the source themselves.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="10823_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Copying text directly from a source describes quoting, which still requires a citation. Searching for a library database is part of the research process, not citation. Summarizing the main points is a method of using source material, not the act of crediting it. Citation is the formal acknowledgment that the information or ideas came from another person's work.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="67663_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Copying text directly from a source describes quoting, which still requires a citation. Searching for a library database is part of the research process, not citation. Summarizing the main points is a method of using source material, not the act of crediting it. Citation is the formal acknowledgment that the information or ideas came from another person's work.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="89609_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Copying text directly from a source describes quoting, which still requires a citation. Searching for a library database is part of the research process, not citation. Summarizing the main points is a method of using source material, not the act of crediting it. Citation is the formal acknowledgment that the information or ideas came from another person's work.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="ged5ffd21ec184f81de2148b908c0f056" title="Question 19">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>64167,72204,91895,61097</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is the purpose of an interview write-up?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="64167">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To present information gathered from an interview in an organized, readable format</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="72204">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To record every question and answer from the interview in exact order</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="91895">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To replace the need for academic sources in a research paper</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="61097">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To summarize only the interviewer's observations and opinions</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">64167</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="64167_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">72204</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="72204_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">91895</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="91895_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">61097</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="61097_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">64167</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="64167_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The purpose of an interview write-up is to present information gathered from an interview in an organized, readable format. It shares insights with readers and helps them understand what you learned from the conversation, written in narrative paragraph form rather than a question-and-answer transcript.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="72204_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Recording every question and answer in exact order produces a transcript, not a write-up. An interview write-up does not replace academic sources—it serves as a primary source that can be combined with other research. The write-up focuses on what the subject shared, not on the interviewer's personal opinions. The goal is to tell the subject's story clearly and accurately.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="91895_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Recording every question and answer in exact order produces a transcript, not a write-up. An interview write-up does not replace academic sources—it serves as a primary source that can be combined with other research. The write-up focuses on what the subject shared, not on the interviewer's personal opinions. The goal is to tell the subject's story clearly and accurately.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="61097_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Recording every question and answer in exact order produces a transcript, not a write-up. An interview write-up does not replace academic sources—it serves as a primary source that can be combined with other research. The write-up focuses on what the subject shared, not on the interviewer's personal opinions. The goal is to tell the subject's story clearly and accurately.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
