    <item ident="ga3c3de85831e8aa4c62ab0e91ffa6722" title="Question 20">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>35061,49308,48459,85090</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What should you do with your interview notes immediately after an interview ends?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="35061">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Review and clarify them while the conversation is still fresh in your memory</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="49308">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Delete any information that seems unimportant</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="48459">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Send the notes to your interviewee for approval before using them</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="85090">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Wait until you are ready to write your paper before reading them again</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">35061</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="35061_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">49308</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="49308_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">48459</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="48459_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">85090</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="85090_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">35061</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="35061_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">You should review and clarify your interview notes immediately after the interview while the conversation is still fresh in your memory. Details fade quickly, and reviewing notes right away allows you to fill in gaps, correct errors, and capture important context before it is forgotten.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="49308_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Deleting information too early may cause you to lose details that become important later. Sending notes to the interviewee for approval is not a standard step in the research process. Waiting until you are ready to write before reviewing your notes about risks losing accuracy and detail. Reviewing notes promptly is one of the most important practices for producing a high-quality interview write-up.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="48459_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Deleting information too early may cause you to lose details that become important later. Sending notes to the interviewee for approval is not a standard step in the research process. Waiting until you are ready to write before reviewing your notes about risks losing accuracy and detail. Reviewing notes promptly is one of the most important practices for producing a high-quality interview write-up.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="85090_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Deleting information too early may cause you to lose details that become important later. Sending notes to the interviewee for approval is not a standard step in the research process. Waiting until you are ready to write before reviewing your notes about risks losing accuracy and detail. Reviewing notes promptly is one of the most important practices for producing a high-quality interview write-up.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gcb9f58ab550aa695d7b84d36fb122d9b" title="Question 21">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>95822,76380,62653,33117</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is a secondary source?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="95822">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A source that discusses, interprets, or analyzes information from primary materials</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="76380">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A source that provides firsthand information from the original event or person</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="62653">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A source that is always less reliable than a primary source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="33117">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A source that can only be found in a library database</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">95822</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="95822_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">76380</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="76380_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">62653</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="62653_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">33117</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="33117_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">95822</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="95822_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">A secondary source is a source that discusses, interprets, or analyzes information from primary materials. Examples include magazine articles, biographies, literary reviews, and television documentaries. Secondary sources are one step removed from the original information.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="76380_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A source that provides firsthand information from the original event or person describes a primary source, not a secondary source. Secondary sources are not always less reliable than primary sources—a well-conducted secondary analysis may be more trustworthy than a poorly designed primary study. Secondary sources are not limited to library databases; they can be found in many places. The defining feature of a secondary source is that it interprets or builds upon primary material.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="62653_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A source that provides firsthand information from the original event or person describes a primary source, not a secondary source. Secondary sources are not always less reliable than primary sources—a well-conducted secondary analysis may be more trustworthy than a poorly designed primary study. Secondary sources are not limited to library databases; they can be found in many places. The defining feature of a secondary source is that it interprets or builds upon primary material.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="33117_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A source that provides firsthand information from the original event or person describes a primary source, not a secondary source. Secondary sources are not always less reliable than primary sources—a well-conducted secondary analysis may be more trustworthy than a poorly designed primary study. Secondary sources are not limited to library databases; they can be found in many places. The defining feature of a secondary source is that it interprets or builds upon primary material.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g6b458b8bb1c925eda6ed7b9a3bcc67f1" title="Question 22">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>93159,23663,36519,25514</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the definition of a summary in research writing?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="93159">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A concise restatement of a source's main points in your own words</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="23663">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A word-for-word reproduction of a source placed in quotation marks</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="36519">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A complete restatement of a source using new sentence structure</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="25514">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A list of all sources used in a research paper</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">93159</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="93159_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">23663</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="23663_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">36519</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="36519_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">25514</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="25514_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">93159</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="93159_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary is a concise restatement of a source's main points in your own words. Summarizing works best when only the major ideas are relevant to your paper or when complex information needs to be reduced to a few key points for your readers.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="23663_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A word-for-word reproduction placed in quotation marks describes a direct quotation. A complete restatement using a new sentence structure at the same level of detail describes paraphrasing. A list of all sources used describes a reference list. Summarizing differs from both paraphrasing and quoting because it greatly reduces the length of the original material and focuses only on the most essential ideas.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="36519_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A word-for-word reproduction placed in quotation marks describes a direct quotation. A complete restatement using a new sentence structure at the same level of detail describes paraphrasing. A list of all sources used describes a reference list. Summarizing differs from both paraphrasing and quoting because it greatly reduces the length of the original material and focuses only on the most essential ideas.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="25514_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A word-for-word reproduction placed in quotation marks describes a direct quotation. A complete restatement using a new sentence structure at the same level of detail describes paraphrasing. A list of all sources used describes a reference list. Summarizing differs from both paraphrasing and quoting because it greatly reduces the length of the original material and focuses only on the most essential ideas.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gade046629c0991e35a1c406a5d9a2fc6" title="Question 23">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>16862,85832,62090,82267</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which of the following describes the &lt;strong&gt;thesaurus method&lt;/strong&gt; of paraphrasing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="16862">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Replacing words with synonyms while keeping the original sentence structure</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="85832">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Restating an idea using completely new wording and sentence structure</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="62090">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Condensing a long passage into one or two sentences</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="82267">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Integrating a direct quote into your own complete sentence</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">16862</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="16862_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">85832</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="85832_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">62090</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="62090_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">82267</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="82267_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">16862</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="16862_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;thesaurus method&lt;/strong&gt; describes replacing words with synonyms while keeping the original sentence structure. This approach is considered a form of plagiarism because it does not represent original thinking or demonstrate genuine understanding of the source material.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="85832_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Restating an idea using completely new wording and sentence structure describes correct paraphrasing. Condensing a long passage into one or two sentences describes summarizing. Integrating a direct quote into your own sentence describes proper quote integration. True paraphrasing requires completely restructuring the sentence and rewriting it in your own voice, not simply swapping out individual words.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="62090_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Restating an idea using completely new wording and sentence structure describes correct paraphrasing. Condensing a long passage into one or two sentences describes summarizing. Integrating a direct quote into your own sentence describes proper quote integration. True paraphrasing requires completely restructuring the sentence and rewriting it in your own voice, not simply swapping out individual words.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="82267_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Restating an idea using completely new wording and sentence structure describes correct paraphrasing. Condensing a long passage into one or two sentences describes summarizing. Integrating a direct quote into your own sentence describes proper quote integration. True paraphrasing requires completely restructuring the sentence and rewriting it in your own voice, not simply swapping out individual words.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="ge51d06cf6711d2a4cee4268cef363316" title="Question 24">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>2666,84536,69538,47718</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is a reference list in APA style?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="2666">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A list at the end of a paper that contains full citation details for every source used</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="84536">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A collection of notes taken during the research process</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="69538">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A list of search terms used to find sources online</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="47718">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary of the main points covered in a research paper</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">2666</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="2666_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">84536</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="84536_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69538</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="69538_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">47718</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="47718_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">2666</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="2666_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A reference list in APA style is a list at the end of a paper that contains full citation details for every source used. Every in-text citation in the paper must have a matching entry in the reference list so readers can locate the original source.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="84536_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A collection of research notes is part of the research process but is not a reference list. A list of search terms is a research strategy tool, not a citation document. A summary of main points describes a conclusion or abstract. In APA style, every source cited within the paper must appear in the reference list, and every reference list entry must correspond to a source cited in the paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="69538_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A collection of research notes is part of the research process but is not a reference list. A list of search terms is a research strategy tool, not a citation document. A summary of main points describes a conclusion or abstract. In APA style, every source cited within the paper must appear in the reference list, and every reference list entry must correspond to a source cited in the paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="47718_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A collection of research notes is part of the research process but is not a reference list. A list of search terms is a research strategy tool, not a citation document. A summary of main points describes a conclusion or abstract. In APA style, every source cited within the paper must appear in the reference list, and every reference list entry must correspond to a source cited in the paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g4af6c4ac8c3652eb3c193f8ee046aa26" title="Question 25">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>69789,45763,38811,56625</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which of the following best describes an in-text citation in APA format?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="69789">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The author's last name and year of publication placed in parentheses within the text</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="45763">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The full title of the source placed at the end of each sentence</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="38811">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A footnote placed at the bottom of the page with the source details</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="56625">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The author's first and last name written at the beginning of each paragraph</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69789</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="69789_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">45763</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="45763_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">38811</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="38811_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">56625</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="56625_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69789</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="69789_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">An in-text citation in APA format places the author's last name and year of publication in parentheses within the text, at the end of the sentence that uses the source. This format allows readers to connect the cited information to the full reference list entry.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45763_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Placing the full title of the source at the end of each sentence is not standard APA format. Footnotes at the bottom of the page are used in some other citation styles, such as Chicago, but not in APA. Writing the author's full name at the beginning of each paragraph does not follow APA conventions. APA in-text citations use a brief parenthetical format—last name and year—to keep the text readable while still crediting the source.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="38811_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Placing the full title of the source at the end of each sentence is not standard APA format. Footnotes at the bottom of the page are used in some other citation styles, such as Chicago, but not in APA. Writing the author's full name at the beginning of each paragraph does not follow APA conventions. APA in-text citations use a brief parenthetical format—last name and year—to keep the text readable while still crediting the source.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="56625_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Placing the full title of the source at the end of each sentence is not standard APA format. Footnotes at the bottom of the page are used in some other citation styles, such as Chicago, but not in APA. Writing the author's full name at the beginning of each paragraph does not follow APA conventions. APA in-text citations use a brief parenthetical format—last name and year—to keep the text readable while still crediting the source.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g1a5b66acf27b1b24e5505fbdca9c4fb2" title="Question 26">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>33368,6070,2755,92821</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the term for a rough written version of a paper that is not yet in its final form?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="33368">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A draft</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6070">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="2755">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A paraphrase</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="92821">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A reference</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">33368</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="33368_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">6070</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="6070_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">2755</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="2755_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">92821</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="92821_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">33368</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="33368_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A draft is a rough written version of a paper that is not yet in its final form. Drafting is Step 5 in the six-step research writing process, where you combine your research findings with your own critical analysis into an initial version of your paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="6070_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary is a brief restatement of a source's main points. A paraphrase is a restatement of source material in your own words and sentence structure. A reference is the citation that acknowledges a source used in your work. None of these describe the act of producing an initial version of a complete paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="2755_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary is a brief restatement of a source's main points. A paraphrase is a restatement of source material in your own words and sentence structure. A reference is the citation that acknowledges a source used in your work. None of these describe the act of producing an initial version of a complete paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="92821_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary is a brief restatement of a source's main points. A paraphrase is a restatement of source material in your own words and sentence structure. A reference is the citation that acknowledges a source used in your work. None of these describe the act of producing an initial version of a complete paper.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gbfc327bd1940d066b0f55c82341c7cd6" title="Question 27">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>52619,16380,79424,7546</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the main limitation of using popular search engines for academic research?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="52619">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines rank results by popularity rather than accuracy</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="16380">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines only display results from government websites</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="79424">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines require a paid subscription to access results</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="7546">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines cannot find results for academic topics</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">52619</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="52619_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">16380</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="16380_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">79424</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="79424_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">7546</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="7546_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">52619</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="52619_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The main limitation of using popular search engines for academic research is that they rank results by how often websites are visited, not by how accurate or reliable they are. A well-designed but inaccurate website may appear before a credible academic source.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="16380_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines display results from many types of websites, not only government sites. Most popular search engines are free to use. Search engines can find results on nearly any topic, including academic ones. The core problem is that high ranking in search results reflects popularity, not trustworthiness. This is why evaluating each source individually is an important research skill.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="79424_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines display results from many types of websites, not only government sites. Most popular search engines are free to use. Search engines can find results on nearly any topic, including academic ones. The core problem is that high ranking in search results reflects popularity, not trustworthiness. This is why evaluating each source individually is an important research skill.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="7546_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Search engines display results from many types of websites, not only government sites. Most popular search engines are free to use. Search engines can find results on nearly any topic, including academic ones. The core problem is that high ranking in search results reflects popularity, not trustworthiness. This is why evaluating each source individually is an important research skill.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g1afea422fa551d69bf06dad80b663a02" title="Question 28">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>46419,90960,29059,4788</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What type of source is an autobiography?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="46419">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A primary source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="90960">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A secondary source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="29059">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">An unreliable source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="4788">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A tertiary source</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">46419</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="46419_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">90960</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="90960_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">29059</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="29059_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">4788</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="4788_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">46419</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="46419_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">An autobiography is a primary source because it is a firsthand account written by the person who experienced the events described. Like diaries and personal letters, autobiographies provide direct, unfiltered perspectives from the individual themselves.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="90960_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A secondary source involves interpretation or analysis of primary material, which an autobiography does not do—it records the author's own lived experience. An autobiography is not automatically unreliable; reliability depends on the author and context. Tertiary sources compile or summarize secondary sources, such as encyclopedias or textbooks. An autobiography fits the definition of a primary source because the author is the original witness to the events described.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="29059_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A secondary source involves interpretation or analysis of primary material, which an autobiography does not do—it records the author's own lived experience. An autobiography is not automatically unreliable; reliability depends on the author and context. Tertiary sources compile or summarize secondary sources, such as encyclopedias or textbooks. An autobiography fits the definition of a primary source because the author is the original witness to the events described.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="4788_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A secondary source involves interpretation or analysis of primary material, which an autobiography does not do—it records the author's own lived experience. An autobiography is not automatically unreliable; reliability depends on the author and context. Tertiary sources compile or summarize secondary sources, such as encyclopedias or textbooks. An autobiography fits the definition of a primary source because the author is the original witness to the events described.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gc9a246ccf898b4a73928379ee06f8dfb" title="Question 29">
