          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="40704_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">24313</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="24313_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">32390</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="32390_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">96015</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="96015_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Organizing research and ideas, which is Step 4, is when you decide which sources to cite and confirm that the evidence you collected supports your thesis. If your evidence does not support your thesis at this stage, you conduct additional research and adjust your thesis as needed.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="40704_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Conducting research is Step 3, when you gather sources—not when you evaluate whether they support your thesis. Drafting your paper is Step 5, when you begin writing after your research is organized. Revising and editing is Step 6, when you polish the completed draft. Evaluating sources against your thesis is a critical part of Step 4 that must happen before drafting begins.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="24313_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Conducting research is Step 3, when you gather sources—not when you evaluate whether they support your thesis. Drafting your paper is Step 5, when you begin writing after your research is organized. Revising and editing is Step 6, when you polish the completed draft. Evaluating sources against your thesis is a critical part of Step 4 that must happen before drafting begins.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="32390_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Conducting research is Step 3, when you gather sources—not when you evaluate whether they support your thesis. Drafting your paper is Step 5, when you begin writing after your research is organized. Revising and editing is Step 6, when you polish the completed draft. Evaluating sources against your thesis is a critical part of Step 4 that must happen before drafting begins.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
