    <item ident="g77edce7edccc28305b8575d131781d04" title="Question 40">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>5106,45196,17873,41652</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the recommended format for presenting information on a family history project?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="5106">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Full sentences and paragraphs organized under clear section headings</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="45196">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A numbered list of names, dates, and locations for each family member</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="17873">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A question-and-answer transcript of family interviews</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="41652">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A bullet-point outline of key facts about each generation</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">5106</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="5106_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">45196</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="45196_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">17873</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="17873_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">41652</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="41652_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">5106</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="5106_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A family history personal history project should be presented in full sentences and paragraphs organized under clear section headings. This narrative format transforms raw genealogical data into engaging writing that brings your ancestors to life for readers.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45196_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A numbered list of names, dates, and locations presents information without the narrative context that makes family history meaningful and readable. A question-and-answer transcript is the format of a raw interview record, not a finished write-up. A bullet-point outline is a planning tool, not a final document. The assignment specifically requires narrative paragraph form throughout, with headings to organize each section clearly.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="17873_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A numbered list of names, dates, and locations presents information without the narrative context that makes family history meaningful and readable. A question-and-answer transcript is the format of a raw interview record, not a finished write-up. A bullet-point outline is a planning tool, not a final document. The assignment specifically requires narrative paragraph form throughout, with headings to organize each section clearly.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="41652_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A numbered list of names, dates, and locations presents information without the narrative context that makes family history meaningful and readable. A question-and-answer transcript is the format of a raw interview record, not a finished write-up. A bullet-point outline is a planning tool, not a final document. The assignment specifically requires narrative paragraph form throughout, with headings to organize each section clearly.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g13e6aa0264deb42b54aad6f341839734" title="Question 41">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>84827,55719,71112,65107</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the term for a formal meeting in which a person is asked questions to gather research information?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="84827">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">An interview</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="55719">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A survey</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="71112">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A draft</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="65107">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A citation</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">84827</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="84827_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">55719</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="55719_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">71112</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="71112_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">65107</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="65107_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">84827</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="84827_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">An interview is a formal meeting in which a person is asked questions to gather research information. Interviews are a valuable primary source because they provide firsthand information directly from a person with relevant knowledge or experience.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="55719_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A survey is a written set of questions distributed to multiple people, not a formal in-person meeting. A draft is a rough version of a written paper. A citation is the acknowledgment of a source used in your work. Interviews are distinct from other research methods because they allow you to gather direct, personalized responses from a specific individual.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="71112_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A survey is a written set of questions distributed to multiple people, not a formal in-person meeting. A draft is a rough version of a written paper. A citation is the acknowledgment of a source used in your work. Interviews are distinct from other research methods because they allow you to gather direct, personalized responses from a specific individual.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="65107_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A survey is a written set of questions distributed to multiple people, not a formal in-person meeting. A draft is a rough version of a written paper. A citation is the acknowledgment of a source used in your work. Interviews are distinct from other research methods because they allow you to gather direct, personalized responses from a specific individual.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g50b571505ad3060800d6605eb9750d8a" title="Question 42">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>61014,7993,33623,32363</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is the first thing you should do to prepare for a family history interview with a relative?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="61014">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Contact the family member early in the research process and explain your purpose</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="7993">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Begin writing your personal history before conducting the interview</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="33623">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Send your relative a completed draft of the family history for their review</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="32363">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Record the interview without asking for your relative's permission first</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">61014</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="61014_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">7993</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="7993_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">33623</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="33623_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">32363</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="32363_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">61014</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="61014_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The first step in preparing for a family history interview is to contact the family member early in the research process and explain your purpose. Reaching out early gives your relative time to prepare and ensures they understand how their information will be used.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="7993_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Writing your personal history before conducting the interview skips the essential research step of gathering firsthand information. Sending a draft for review is not part of the preparation process—it is not a required step at all. Recording an interview without permission is an ethical violation. The interview process must begin with respectful, transparent communication about your purpose and intentions.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="33623_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Writing your personal history before conducting the interview skips the essential research step of gathering firsthand information. Sending a draft for review is not part of the preparation process—it is not a required step at all. Recording an interview without permission is an ethical violation. The interview process must begin with respectful, transparent communication about your purpose and intentions.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="32363_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Writing your personal history before conducting the interview skips the essential research step of gathering firsthand information. Sending a draft for review is not part of the preparation process—it is not a required step at all. Recording an interview without permission is an ethical violation. The interview process must begin with respectful, transparent communication about your purpose and intentions.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gdab932dc0462b295b3ac53ba19a5f3c3" title="Question 43">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>55840,6126,34587,32105</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What does the W04 reading identify as a &lt;strong&gt;growth accelerator&lt;/strong&gt; use of AI?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="55840">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using AI to help you think more clearly about your own work without replacing your effort</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6126">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using AI to write your research paper from a list of sources you provide</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="34587">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using AI to generate citations for sources you have not read</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="32105">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using AI to paraphrase your source material before you write your paper</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">55840</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="55840_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">6126</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="6126_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">34587</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="34587_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">32105</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="32105_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">55840</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="55840_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">A growth accelerator use of AI means using it to help you think more clearly about your own work without replacing your effort. For example, asking AI to identify gaps in your organized ideas or to check whether your transitions are clear after you have already written your own draft are growth accelerator uses.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="6126_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Asking AI to write your research paper from a list of sources describes a dependence trap—it replaces the intellectual work the course is designed to develop. Asking AI to generate citations for sources you have not read creates a serious academic integrity risk because AI regularly produces fabricated citations. Asking AI to paraphrase your source material before you write is also a dependence trap because it removes the skill of understanding and restating sources in your own words.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="34587_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Asking AI to write your research paper from a list of sources describes a dependence trap—it replaces the intellectual work the course is designed to develop. Asking AI to generate citations for sources you have not read creates a serious academic integrity risk because AI regularly produces fabricated citations. Asking AI to paraphrase your source material before you write is also a dependence trap because it removes the skill of understanding and restating sources in your own words.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="32105_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;Asking AI to write your research paper from a list of sources describes a dependence trap—it replaces the intellectual work the course is designed to develop. Asking AI to generate citations for sources you have not read creates a serious academic integrity risk because AI regularly produces fabricated citations. Asking AI to paraphrase your source material before you write is also a dependence trap because it removes the skill of understanding and restating sources in your own words.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gbd44908be6d8be44300fffb3498be76f" title="Question 44">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
